          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller through an isolated CAN transceiver"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Tying the transceiver grounds together defeats galvanic isolation, allowing ground offsets and transients on the CAN cable side to couple into the controller-side ground.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN transceivers' GND1 and GND2 pins appear tied to the same GND net, defeating the galvanic isolation specified for both CAN interfaces."
